      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "25ebb69a-b8ea-56ca-8346-80e2c5835b02",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cristiana Cucchi, Bazooka Girl\n- Companies: HI-NRG Attack\n- Songs: Velfarre 2000, I Like Chopin\n- Genres: Eurobeat, Italo disco\n- Topics: C-Eurobeat\n\nFacts:\n- Italo disco is a pop music genre that originated in Italy and was mainly produced from the late 1970s to the late 1980s.\n- “I Like Chopin” is generally regarded as one of the most significant Italo disco tracks of the mid-1980s.\n- Cristiana Cucchi, also known as Bazooka Girl and by the Chinese name 郑玉婷, is a eurobeat vocalist.\n- Eurobeat originated from Italo disco.\n- Cristiana Cucchi is one of the most well-known names on HI-NRG Attack, an Italian record label.\n- Cristiana Cucchi’s speedy and energetic songs, especially the English-language Chinese New Year hit “Velfarre 2000,” have charmed many C-Eurobeat fans.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "14ee4d31-7f66-569b-ae05-f0d745a8fa4b",
        "text": "Page: Cristiana Cucchi. Sentence: Bazooka Girl (Chinese: 火箭炮姑娘, Pinyin: Huǒjiànpào gūniang) (real name: Cristiana Cucchi, Chinese: 郑玉婷, Pinyin: Zhèngyùtíng) is a eurobeat (originating from Italo disco) vocalist and one of the most well-known names on \"HI-NRG Attack\", an Italian record label.\nPage: Cristiana Cucchi. Sentence: Her speedy and energetic songs, especially her hit, a Chinese New Year song in English called \"Velfarre 2000\", have charmed many C-Eurobeat fans.\nPage: Italo disco. Sentence: Italo disco (sometimes hyphenated, such as Italo-disco, subjected to varying capitalization, or abbreviated as Italo) is a genre of pop music which originated in Italy and was mainly produced from the late 1970s to the late 1980s.\nPage: I Like Chopin. Sentence: It is generally regarded as one of the most significant Italo disco tracks of the mid-1980s.",
